## Name of the node.
##
## One release boots as a frontend, logic or service node depending on
## its environment, so the name comes from $LYCEUM_NODE_NAME.
##
## The frontend node's name is load-bearing for the Zig client, not
## just cosmetic: zerl's establish_connection/3 builds the target node
## name as "lyceum_server@" ++ <address typed in the client>, so
## whichever node hosts the client-facing gateway has to be started
## with LYCEUM_NODE_NAME=lyceum_server. Renaming it requires a matching
## client change.
##
## Short names also have to stay: zerl inits its C node with
## ei_connect_init, which is short-name mode, and a long-name VM
## refuses those connections. Short names are enough for same-host
## multi-node work, which covers development and the test clusters.
## Going multi-host later means moving the client to
## ei_connect_xinit first.
-sname lyceum_server

## Cookie for distributed Erlang
-setcookie lyceum

## Connect only to the peers in LYCEUM_PEERS, never transitively to
## whatever they are connected to. This is what keeps the layering
## real: a frontend node linked to logic does not learn about the
## service nodes behind it, and `pg` (which never relays across an
## intermediate node) therefore cannot show it a service worker.
-kernel connect_all false

## Extra options
-heart
+K true
+A30

# Erlang Distribution Port Range
-kernel inet_dist_listen_min 9100
-kernel inet_dist_listen_max 9155
